title: 'spec-msg/primitives: Implement Speculative Messaging primitives'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |
    Closes #12346

    New `cumulus-primitives-spec-messaging` crate (`cumulus/primitives/spec-messaging/`),
    `no_std`-compatible, added to workspace members.

    ### `CommitmentSet<const N: u32>`

    Canonical, bounded set of `(ParaId, Hash)` entries for `provides`/`requires` commitments.

    - Manual `Decode` rejects input whose `ParaId`s aren't strictly increasing, preventing
      collator/PVF encoding disagreements.
    - `try_from_iter`: builds from an unordered iterator, sorting by `ParaId`, rejecting
      duplicates (`CommitmentError::DuplicateParaId`) or over-capacity input
      (`CommitmentError::TooManyEntries`).
    - Accessors: `get`, `len`, `is_empty`, `iter`, `IntoIterator`.
    - Full derive set (`Encode`, `Decode`, `DecodeWithMemTracking`, `MaxEncodedLen`, `TypeInfo`, ...).
    - 10 unit tests: sorted construction, duplicate/overflow rejection, encode/decode
      round-trip, decode rejection (out-of-order/duplicate/over-capacity), lookup, iteration, default.

    ### `OutgoingMessage<MaxMsgLen: Get<u32>>`

    - Fields: `source`, `destination`, `position`, bounded `payload: BoundedVec<u8, MaxMsgLen>`,
      full derive set for storage/`UMPSignal` embedding.
    - `hash_leaf()`: produces the MMR leaf hash from the preimage
      `LEAF_TAG ++ LEAF_VERSION ++ source ++ destination ++ position.to_le_bytes() ++
      (payload.len() as u32).to_le_bytes() ++ payload` via `blake2_256` — matches the
      issue's specified preimage format exactly.
    - 7 unit tests: constructor, determinism, exact preimage (known-answer test), per-field
      hash sensitivity (source/destination/position/payload).

    ### MMR operations (`mmr.rs`)

    Rather than hand-rolling an accumulator, this crate plugs into
    `polkadot-ckb-merkle-mountain-range` (`mmr_lib`), already an audited `no_std` workspace
    dependency exposed via `sp-mmr-primitives`. The crate contributes a single adapter:

    - `SpecMerge` — implements `mmr_lib::Merge` with domain-tagged `blake2_256` hashing:
      - `merge(l, r)` → `blake2_256(INNER_TAG ++ l ++ r)` (inner tree nodes)
      - `merge_peaks(l, r)` → `blake2_256(PEAK_TAG ++ l ++ r)` (peak bagging)
    - Domain separation constants: `LEAF_TAG`, `INNER_TAG`, `PEAK_TAG`, `LEAF_VERSION` —
      prevent hash collisions across node types and protocol versions.

    Callers build an accumulator directly with `mmr_lib::MMR<Hash, SpecMerge, S>`, gaining
    multi-leaf inclusion proofs (`gen_proof` / `MerkleProof::verify`) and append-only
    extension proofs (`gen_ancestry_proof` / `verify_incremental`) from the library at no
    extra implementation cost.

    - 6 unit tests: empty MMR, root determinism, per-append root change, `merge` order
      sensitivity, `merge_peaks` order sensitivity, domain tag isolation (inner vs peak).

    ### Notes

    - `OutgoingMessage` includes a `source: ParaId` field not present in the issue's struct
      sketch — required because the issue's own leaf-preimage format includes
      `source_parachain`, which the struct must carry to compute `hash_leaf()`.
    - `mmr_lib` bags peaks pairwise right-to-left via `merge_peaks(right, left)`, whereas a
      naive single-call implementation would hash all peaks together. The roots differ for
      3+ peaks.
crates:
- name: cumulus-primitives-spec-messaging
  bump: major
